{"type":"message","id":"b91d128b","parentId":"5ec9ce12","timestamp":"2026-06-02T09:12:31.010Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"用户在问存在哪了。TOOLS.md里的GitHub token部分我写的是 `ghp_8v…T0KR`，这不对，他给的是完整token但中间打了省略号。我应该更新成完整token。\n","thinkingSignature":"dbf0eb8609b40a8eaa9ab103fe653f23f1c8f89344396a86ef1671913efcc3b6"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nTOOLS.md，但刚才存的时候中间部分我打码了（你发的被省略了），来，把完整token发我，或者告诉我你自己去拿哪里找。"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":28035,"output":84,"cacheRead":96,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":28215,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1780391546171,"responseId":"066dd17b11dd5f0a24373f312fc0c9e2"}}
{"type":"message","id":"a6d7c2b2","parentId":"b91d128b","timestamp":"2026-06-02T09:15:46.950Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Conversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"chat_id\": \"user:ou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff\",\n  \"message_id\": \"om_x100b6eddbd271c88c3b2804fad78831\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"ou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff\",\n  \"sender\": \"ou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Tue 2026-06-02 09:15 UTC\"\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"ou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff\",\n  \"id\": \"ou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff\",\n  \"name\": \"ou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff\"\n}\n```\n\n[message_id: om_x100b6eddbd271c88c3b2804fad78831]\nou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff: GitHub token不能配置到GitHub的配置文件里嘛"}],"timestamp":1780391746916}}
{"type":"message","id":"b85ea73b","parentId":"a6d7c2b2","timestamp":"2026-06-02T09:15:50.921Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking whether the GitHub token can be configured in GitHub's configuration file (~/.gitconfig or ~/.config/gh/). Let me think about this.\n\nGitHub's CLI tool `gh` uses stored credentials. But `gh` uses OAuth, not personal access tokens directly. For git operations using HTTPS, you can use `gh auth login` or configure credential helper.\n\nActually, the user might be asking about storing the token in git's credential helper or netrc file. Or they might be asking about GitHub's `gh` CLI configuration.\n\nLet me think about the simplest approach:\n1. For git operations via HTTPS, you can use credential helper: `git config --global credential.helper cache`\n\n\n2. Or store in `~/.git-credentials`\n3. Or use `gh auth login` with the token\n\nBut the simplest way for the token to be usable would be configuring it in gh's auth or git's credential storage. I should give a direct answer on what's practical here.","thinkingSignature":"4ed787d73ddd10563c90279f4b83d1d0b119fa5df4b8a92c22e77e242f27f525"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n可以。最简单的方式：\n\n```bash\ngh auth login --with-token\n```\n\n然后把token粘进去。或者直接写进git配置：\n\n```bash\ngit config --global credential.helper store\n```\n\n之后第一次pull会提示输入用户名密码，用户名填GitHub用户名，密码填token。之后就不用每次输入了。\n\n你希望我用哪种方式配置？"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":394,"output":278,"cacheRead":27840,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":28512,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1780391747006,"responseId":"066dd2438122b078a4f8cf492310b80a"}}
{"type":"message","id":"3e193019","parentId":"b85ea73b","timestamp":"2026-06-02T09:17:10.485Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Conversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"chat_id\": \"user:ou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff\",\n  \"message_id\": \"om_x100b6eddb7c44108c24a0dc8386aed3\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"ou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff\",\n  \"sender\": \"ou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Tue 2026-06-02 09:17 UTC\"\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"ou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff\",\n  \"id\": \"ou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff\",\n  \"name\": \"ou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff\"\n}\n```\n\n[message_id: om_x100b6eddb7c44108c24a0dc8386aed3]\nou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff: 哪个好"}],"timestamp":1780391830455}}
{"type":"message","id":"31914fbf","parentId":"3e193019","timestamp":"2026-06-02T09:17:16.305Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking which method is better for configuring the GitHub token. Let me think about this.\n\n1. `gh auth login --with-token` - This is the official GitHub CLI way. It authenticates the `gh` tool itself, which is used for issues, PRs, etc.\n\n2. `git config --global credential.helper store` - This configures git to store credentials (username + token) in a file. When you do git operations (clone, push, pull), it will prompt once and then store them.\n\nFor the user's use case - they're configuring a token so that Talus (the agent) can use GitHub operations. The `gh` CLI is what OpenClaw skill for GitHub uses. So `gh auth login` would be the more appropriate choice for GitHub operations via the `gh` CLI.\n\n\nBut if they just need plain `git clone` and basic git operations to work, the credential helper approach would suffice. Since they mentioned OpenClaw is already using the `gh` skill, `gh auth login --with-token` is the better recommendation.\n","thinkingSignature":"b0aa1731db100f65bbfe13151a613b4eee1be100349f46fbc02cba5cb2469fd2"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n`gh auth login --with-token` 更好。原因：\n\n1. **专为CLI设计** — `gh` 就是GitHub官方CLI，token认证后`gh issue`、`gh pr`这些命令直接用\n2. **更安全** — token存在系统keychain，不落磁盘\n3. **OpenClaw的GitHub skill就是调`gh`命令** — 配了这个才能正常工作\n\n直接配置命令：\n\n```bash\necho \"ghp_8v…T0KR\" | gh auth login --with-token\n```\n\n要我跑一下吗？"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":464,"output":364,"cacheRead":27904,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":28732,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1780391830550,"responseId":"066dd297e6803e22fe6c3bb9f8d2d715"}}
{"type":"message","id":"4bf92b6b","parentId":"31914fbf","timestamp":"2026-06-02T09:17:54.654Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Conversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"chat_id\": \"user:ou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff\",\n  \"message_id\": \"om_x100b6eddb512d4a8c26b76e00271c66\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"ou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff\",\n  \"sender\": \"ou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Tue 2026-06-02 09:17 UTC\"\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"ou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff\",\n  \"id\": \"ou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff\",\n  \"name\": \"ou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff\"\n}\n```\n\n[message_id: om_x100b6eddb512d4a8c26b76e00271c66]\nou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff: 你在docker里跑了能长久生效么"}],"timestamp":1780391874617}}
{"type":"message","id":"0e9f9714","parentId":"4bf92b6b","timestamp":"2026-06-02T09:17:59.368Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The boss is asking whether running `gh auth login` inside the Docker container will persist - i.e., will the authentication survive container restarts/recreation.\n\nThis is a good question. Docker containers are ephemeral by default - any state inside the container is lost when the container is recreated. So if the token is stored inside the container's filesystem or memory, it won't persist across restarts.\n\nHowever, `gh auth login` typically stores credentials in the host's keychain (like OS keychain) or in `~/.config/gh/` on Linux. The question is whether this storage is on the host volume-mounted into the container, or inside the container's own filesystem.\n\n\nThe key question is whether the OpenClaw workspace directory, where `gh` stores its config, is mounted from the host or ephemeral. If it's a volume mount, credentials persist; if not, they're lost on container recreation. I should configure `gh auth login` and verify where the credentials end up being stored to give a definitive answer.","thinkingSignature":"82ee3620024285b2be4daad1dc58495d3d153cb0a416f419a30ce010d92c83ef"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n好问题。Docker容器是临时文件系统，关机/重启会丢。\n\n要看你OpenClaw的workspace目录有没有做volume挂载——如果是从宿主机挂进去的（如`~/.openclaw`映射到宿主机），那认证状态会保留。\n\n简单验证：\n\n```bash\ndocker inspect openclaw --format '{{json .Mounts}}' | grep -i openclaw\n```\n\n如果workspace目录在宿主机上跑了`gh auth login`，重启后还生效。否则每次都要重新登。\n\n你有办法跑一下看看结果吗？或者告诉我你的docker compose怎么配的，我帮你判断。"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":488,"output":329,"cacheRead":28064,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":28881,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1780391874711,"responseId":"066dd2c3d78d3a3e1ef6171a3c9cde95"}}
