{"type":"message","id":"1e0c05c6","parentId":"588e753b","timestamp":"2026-06-02T09:22:07.112Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The workspace and .openclaw are bind-mounted from the host. So if I run `gh auth login` inside the container, the credentials would persist as long as they land in the host's ~/.openclaw directory (which is bind-mounted). \n\nHowever, `gh auth login` typically stores credentials in the system keychain or ~/.config/gh/, which might not be in the bind-mounted area. Let me think about where `gh` stores its credentials.\n\n`gh` stores config in `~/.config/gh/` directory. In the container, that would be `/home/node/.config/gh/`. But the bind mount is `/home/ubuntu/.openclaw` → `/home/node/.openclaw`, so `~/.config/gh/` (which is outside the openclaw dir) won't persist.\n\n\nThe best approach would be to explicitly set the `GH_CONFIG_DIR` environment variable to point to the bind-mounted directory so the credentials actually persist, rather than relying on the default config location.\n","thinkingSignature":"d93353b04dfcf364105df226c8b50572b74ff35e6830c27e28935ecaed0aea27"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nworkspace和.openclaw都挂载了，但`gh`的配置存在`~/.config/gh/`——这个目录没挂载，所以重启后会丢。\n\n解决方案：把gh配置目录也挂进去，或者用环境变量指向挂载目录。\n\n**方案一**：创建目录并挂载（改docker-compose）\n\n**方案二**：直接跑命令验证是否能工作，能用就先这样\n\n你想用哪种？还是先验证一下`gh auth status`看看现在容器里gh登录状态？"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":630,"output":297,"cacheRead":28672,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":29599,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1780392122170,"responseId":"066dd3ba8f6a83f642c2e3dc5a0f01cd"}}
