{"type":"message","id":"749d5e4c","parentId":"0a10ef81","timestamp":"2026-06-02T09:23:18.312Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is checking gh auth status from the host machine (ubuntu), not inside the Docker container. Also gh is not installed on the host.\n\nKey findings:\n1. gh is not installed on the host machine (only \"gitsome\" apt package is suggested)\n2. gh config directory doesn't exist yet\n\nLet me think about what to do:\n1. The OpenClaw workspace is mounted at /home/ubuntu/.openclaw/workspace\n2. gh config would be at ~/.config/gh/ on the host - but this dir doesn't exist yet\n3. gh needs to be installed on the host OR we can exec into the container to run gh\n\nActually, the user is on the HOST machine (ubuntu), not inside the Docker container. \n\nI'm realizing the skill uses gh CLI commands, so I need to either install gh on the host machine or exec into the container where the skill runs. Since the workspace is mounted from the host, I could also configure git credential storage there. Let me install gh first since that's the cleanest approach for the GitHub skill to work properly.","thinkingSignature":"3036fc498fe156e4fe5cb9058456dc536d6dfd3b8ebf6801b1cfd75cf9e7afd0"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n`gh`没装，装一下：\n\n```bash\nsudo apt install gh\n```\n\n装完再运行：\n\n```bash\ngh auth status\n```\n\n或者你要嫌麻烦，也可以直接在workspace目录配置git credential，不用装`gh`：\n\n```bash\ngit config --global credential.helper \"store --file /home/ubuntu/.openclaw/workspace/.git-credentials\"\n```\n\n这样token会存到workspace目录，重启不丢。你选哪个？"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":746,"output":314,"cacheRead":28800,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":29860,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1780392193222,"responseId":"066dd40142ea00652676bb1ddfed1e0f"}}
